    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312391/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Neith had a tea here, to which came the Fenellosas, Steffens, Hodder and I forget who, Norman among others. We dined alone with the Alexanders - very pleasant. Their house is awfully nice.
***
Thursday Dec. 17. 03 .
I was rather low, so Bernhard went alone to call on Mr. Lathrop in his studio. We met at Mr. Hyde’s for lunch, with a Miss Platt, Mr. Gregory and Cottenett. Hyde is rather handsome and bumptious, with  no taste . He is very young. Paid some calls. Dined with Chapmans (Mr. and Mrs. Lawrence) at 7, and went to Concert of old Music after. Bernhard has developed a most awful cold, one of his very worst!"""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 121 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

